{"title":"AA similarity","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Theorem:\nIn two triangles, if two pairs of corresponding angles are congruent, then the triangles are similar.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AA_similarity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let ABC and DEF be two triangles such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f6862c019809ba2e2e7e7957e3919a6339b21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = \\angle D$\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e8b21da82f5bfe84cd2f697584a78f6ce04534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\angle E$\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" />.\nThe sum interior angles of a triangle is equal to 180. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60e5dd4973cd1e9bd36c7766143179f21b96283d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle C = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab484372c64c42ee508b27773bacf708ccc0357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle D + \\angle E + \\angle F = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"178\" height=\"14\" />.\nWe can write the equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe35e675ba7f0703045904a379d7a29f548fe36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A  + \\angle B + \\angle C = 180 = \\angle D + \\angle E + \\angle F \\Longrightarrow \\angle D + \\angle E + \\angle C = \\angle D + \\angle E + \\angle F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"648\" height=\"16\" />, acknowledging the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02f6862c019809ba2e2e7e7957e3919a6339b21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = \\angle D$\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e8b21da82f5bfe84cd2f697584a78f6ce04534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\angle E$\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" />.\nTo conclude, by subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a811feebefe2d71208aed27f092ddcdabff1751e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle D + \\angle E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> by both equations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c5fb04bc1f2d942745ce50839665101a410eae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C = \\angle F$\" width=\"78\" height=\"12\" />. Since the three angles are congruent, the two triangles are similar.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AA_similarity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Similarity_(geometry)\" title=\"Similarity (geometry)\">Similarity (geometry)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=SAS_similarity\" title=\"SAS similarity\">SAS similarity</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=SSS_similarity\" title=\"SSS similarity\">SSS similarity</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=AA_similarity&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018071834\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 57/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 280/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1729/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.269      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.269      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14389:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018071834 and revision id 292206. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}